{:edb/db-before-t 1519 :edb/db-after-t 1520 :edb/tx-data [[13194139534832 50 #inst "2026-10-08T08:22:08.251Z" 13194139534832 true] [17592186175863 1020 #edb/ref 17592186313224 13194139534832 true] [17592186175863 1020 #edb/ref 17592186313231 13194139534832 true] [17592186176021 1020 #edb/ref 17592186313238 13194139534832 true] [17592186176021 1020 #edb/ref 17592186313245 13194139534832 true] [17592186176021 1020 #edb/ref 17592186313250 13194139534832 true] [17592186313224 1017 #edb/ref 17592186313225 13194139534832 true] [17592186313224 1089 "q-109289" 13194139534832 true] [17592186313224 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045464 13194139534832 true] [17592186313224 1100 "The displacement $s,$ in meters, relative to a fixed origin $O$ of a particle moving in a straight line along the $x$-axis is given by $s(t)=\\sqrt{t}\\,\\operatorname{ln}⁡t,$ where $t>0$ is the time measured in seconds. Determine the time intervals in which the particle is moving in the direction of decreasing $x.$" 13194139534832 true] [17592186313224 1113 #uuid "50f47d99-0d29-59c2-bb2e-982faa827891" 13194139534832 true] [17592186313224 1145 "If the particle moves in the direction of decreasing $x,$ then its velocity is negative. \n\nFirst, we calculate the velocity function by differentiating the position function:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}s}{\\text{d}t} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\sqrt{t}\\,\\operatorname{ln}⁡t) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡t}{2\\sqrt{t}}+\\frac{\\sqrt{t}}{t} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡t}{2\\sqrt{t}}+\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{t}} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡t+2}{2\\sqrt{t}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo calculate time intervals in which the particle is moving in the direction of decreasing $x$, we solve the inequality $v(t)<0:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v(t) & <0 \\\\ \\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡t+2}{2\\sqrt{t}} & <0 \\\\ \\operatorname{ln}⁡t+2 & <0 \\\\ \\operatorname{ln}⁡t & <-2 \\\\ t & <{e}^{-2} \\\\ t & <\\frac{1}{{e}^{2}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the time interval in which the particle is moving to the direction of decreasing $x$ is $t\\in (0,\\frac{1}{{e}^{2}}).$" 13194139534832 true] [17592186313225 1000 #edb/ref 17592186313226 13194139534832 true] [17592186313225 1000 #edb/ref 17592186313227 13194139534832 true] [17592186313225 1000 #edb/ref 17592186313228 13194139534832 true] [17592186313225 1000 #edb/ref 17592186313229 13194139534832 true] [17592186313225 1000 #edb/ref 17592186313230 13194139534832 true] [17592186313225 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534832 true] [17592186313225 1041 "selection" 13194139534832 true] [17592186313225 1104 #edb/ref 17592186313227 13194139534832 true] [17592186313225 1110 #uuid "1bdadce8-c65a-5ba9-962b-2b2deff8f5d8" 13194139534832 true] [17592186313226 1034 "(\\frac{1}{{e}^{2}},\\infty )" 13194139534832 true] [17592186313226 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534832 true] [17592186313226 1111 #uuid "d20b8dd4-3ddd-55b3-86fb-83375e88024f" 13194139534832 true] [17592186313227 1034 "(0,\\frac{1}{{e}^{2}})" 13194139534832 true] [17592186313227 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534832 true] [17592186313227 1111 #uuid "a41cbfb8-13e7-5a6a-a618-8f4d2b734f6b" 13194139534832 true] [17592186313228 1034 "(1,e)" 13194139534832 true] [17592186313228 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534832 true] [17592186313228 1111 #uuid "82692d2c-fd1e-5b01-b3cb-6c8a0df337ba" 13194139534832 true] [17592186313229 1034 "(e,\\infty )" 13194139534832 true] [17592186313229 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534832 true] [17592186313229 1111 #uuid "e2935a20-1892-5012-9267-697c870c8e06" 13194139534832 true] [17592186313230 1034 "(0,\\frac{2}{e})" 13194139534832 true] [17592186313230 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534832 true] [17592186313230 1111 #uuid "327e9d84-65fe-5e64-abf1-9e0e1ec85e54" 13194139534832 true] [17592186313231 1017 #edb/ref 17592186313232 13194139534832 true] [17592186313231 1089 "q-109290" 13194139534832 true] [17592186313231 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139534832 true] [17592186313231 1100 "The displacement $s,$ in meters, relative to a fixed origin $O$ of a particle moving in a straight line along the $x$-axis is given by $s(t)=t{e}^{-t},$ where $t>0$ is the time measured in seconds. Determine the time intervals in which the particle is moving in the direction of decreasing $x.$" 13194139534832 true] [17592186313231 1113 #uuid "2912d1ed-8c93-531d-8d23-8555cf0ff32d" 13194139534832 true] [17592186313231 1145 "If the particle moves in the direction of decreasing $x,$ then its velocity is negative. \n\nFirst, we calculate the velocity function by differentiating the position function:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}s}{\\text{d}t} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(t{e}^{-t}) \\\\  & ={e}^{-t}-t{e}^{-t} \\\\  & =(1-t){e}^{-t}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo calculate time intervals in which the particle is moving in the direction of decreasing $x$, we solve the inequality $v(t)<0:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v(t) & <0 \\\\ (1-t){e}^{-t} & <0 \\\\ 1-t & <0 \\\\ t & >1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the time interval in which the particle is moving to the direction of decreasing $x$ is $t\\in (1,\\infty ).$" 13194139534832 true] [17592186313232 1000 #edb/ref 17592186313233 13194139534832 true] [17592186313232 1000 #edb/ref 17592186313234 13194139534832 true] [17592186313232 1000 #edb/ref 17592186313235 13194139534832 true] [17592186313232 1000 #edb/ref 17592186313236 13194139534832 true] [17592186313232 1000 #edb/ref 17592186313237 13194139534832 true] [17592186313232 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534832 true] [17592186313232 1041 "selection" 13194139534832 true] [17592186313232 1104 #edb/ref 17592186313237 13194139534832 true] [17592186313232 1110 #uuid "3b305db0-a24f-59f4-9972-7b09dd35b380" 13194139534832 true] [17592186313233 1034 "(0,1)" 13194139534832 true] [17592186313233 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534832 true] [17592186313233 1111 #uuid "82e30da0-c514-5d6b-a4f2-32b57f53eeab" 13194139534832 true] [17592186313234 1034 "(1,e)" 13194139534832 true] [17592186313234 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534832 true] [17592186313234 1111 #uuid "feb1851d-1cdc-5e66-b8be-5e49f929eb6f" 13194139534832 true] [17592186313235 1034 "(e,\\infty )" 13194139534832 true] [17592186313235 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534832 true] [17592186313235 1111 #uuid "13ed8951-f25a-51bc-80b8-2224b159127c" 13194139534832 true] [17592186313236 1034 "(0,\\frac{1}{e})" 13194139534832 true] [17592186313236 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534832 true] [17592186313236 1111 #uuid "c3741a95-9af5-5d6c-82c3-c2495ede1033" 13194139534832 true] [17592186313237 1034 "(1,\\infty )" 13194139534832 true] [17592186313237 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534832 true] [17592186313237 1111 #uuid "0b552bf9-1beb-5221-a168-63e371ef621b" 13194139534832 true] [17592186313238 1017 #edb/ref 17592186313239 13194139534832 true] [17592186313238 1089 "q-109307" 13194139534832 true] [17592186313238 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139534832 true] [17592186313238 1100 "A particle $P$ is traveling along the $x$-axis with displacement $s(t)$ from a fixed origin $O$ given by\n\n$$\ns(t)=7{t}^{2}-{t}^{3},\\,t\\ge 0.\n$$\n\nFind the time at which the acceleration is zero, and find the value of the velocity at this moment." 13194139534832 true] [17592186313238 1113 #uuid "7704a427-55d1-5f8e-bf57-d941d8544127" 13194139534832 true] [17592186313238 1145 "First, we calculate $v(t)$ by differentiating $s(t):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}s}{\\text{d}t} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(7{t}^{2}-{t}^{3}) \\\\  & =14t-3{t}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we differentiate $v(t)$ to find $a(t):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}t} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(14t-3{t}^{2}) \\\\  & =14-6t\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we put $a=0$ to find the time when the acceleration is zero:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}14-6t & =0 \\\\ -6t & =-14 \\\\ t & =\\frac{7}{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, the acceleration is zero when $t=\\frac{7}{3}.$ To find the velocity at this moment, we substitute this back into $v(t)$ to get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v(\\frac{7}{3}) & =14(\\frac{7}{3})-3{(\\frac{7}{3})}^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{98}{3}-\\frac{49}{3} \\\\  & =\\frac{49}{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534832 true] [17592186313239 1000 #edb/ref 17592186313240 13194139534832 true] [17592186313239 1000 #edb/ref 17592186313241 13194139534832 true] [17592186313239 1000 #edb/ref 17592186313242 13194139534832 true] [17592186313239 1000 #edb/ref 17592186313243 13194139534832 true] [17592186313239 1000 #edb/ref 17592186313244 13194139534832 true] [17592186313239 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534832 true] [17592186313239 1041 "selection" 13194139534832 true] [17592186313239 1104 #edb/ref 17592186313242 13194139534832 true] [17592186313239 1110 #uuid "5771e197-f85c-5afa-a2e0-a3495933c4d4" 13194139534832 true] [17592186313240 1034 "t=\\frac{3}{2},\\,v=-\\frac{9}{2}" 13194139534832 true] [17592186313240 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534832 true] [17592186313240 1111 #uuid "2a6ae59a-ef01-59d9-be2a-45a738702684" 13194139534832 true] [17592186313241 1034 "t=2,\\,v=-4" 13194139534832 true] [17592186313241 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534832 true] [17592186313241 1111 #uuid "22238f90-983a-58d5-871e-8fa1a5e45d3f" 13194139534832 true] [17592186313242 1034 "t=\\frac{7}{3},\\,v=\\frac{49}{3}" 13194139534832 true] [17592186313242 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534832 true] [17592186313242 1111 #uuid "63cd8d30-4646-5be8-a435-41eb7a14e022" 13194139534832 true] [17592186313243 1034 "t=2,\\,v=6" 13194139534832 true] [17592186313243 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534832 true] [17592186313243 1111 #uuid "583ab37d-d38a-563f-9e91-5b988ae778cb" 13194139534832 true] [17592186313244 1034 "t=\\frac{7}{3},\\,v=\\frac{15}{6}" 13194139534832 true] [17592186313244 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534832 true] [17592186313244 1111 #uuid "4bb0bd13-8b0d-5477-b3ec-c01f9997fc98" 13194139534832 true] [17592186313245 1017 #edb/ref 17592186313246 13194139534832 true] [17592186313245 1017 #edb/ref 17592186313248 13194139534832 true] [17592186313245 1089 "q-335924" 13194139534832 true] [17592186313245 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045464 13194139534832 true] [17592186313245 1100 "A particle $P$ is traveling along the $x$-axis with displacement $s(t)$ from a fixed origin $O$ given by\n\n$$\ns(t)=t\\operatorname{ln}⁡(t)-{t}^{2},\\,t>0.\n$$\n\nFind the time at which the acceleration is zero, and find the value of the velocity at this moment.\n\nThe acceleration is zero at $t=$\n{{field-1}}, and the velocity at this moment is\n$v=$\n{{field-2}}." 13194139534832 true] [17592186313245 1113 #uuid "32a4841d-90ea-5da4-90fb-13141a3fa68d" 13194139534832 true] [17592186313245 1145 "First, we calculate $v(t)$ by differentiating $s(t):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}s}{\\text{d}t} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(t\\operatorname{ln}⁡(t)-{t}^{2}) \\\\  & =1\\cdot \\operatorname{ln}⁡(t)+t\\cdot \\frac{1}{t}-2t \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡(t)+1-2t\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we differentiate $v(t)$ to find $a(t):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}t} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡(t)+1-2t) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{t}-2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we put $a(t)=0$ to find the time when the acceleration is zero:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{t}-2 & =0 \\\\ \\frac{1}{t} & =2 \\\\ t & =\\frac{1}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo the acceleration is zero when $t=\\frac{1}{2}.$ To find the velocity at this moment, we substitute this back into $v(t)$ to get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v\\,(\\frac{1}{2}) & =ln\\,(\\frac{1}{2})+1-2\\cdot \\frac{1}{2} \\\\  & =ln\\,(\\frac{1}{2})+1-1 \\\\  & =ln\\,(\\frac{1}{2}) \\\\  & =-\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the acceleration is zero at $t=\\frac{1}{2},$ and the velocity at this moment is $v=-\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2).$" 13194139534832 true] [17592186313246 1000 #edb/ref 17592186313247 13194139534832 true] [17592186313246 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139534832 true] [17592186313246 1041 "field-1" 13194139534832 true] [17592186313246 1104 #edb/ref 17592186313247 13194139534832 true] [17592186313246 1110 #uuid "a079644d-0ffe-5199-814c-409514ebc282" 13194139534832 true] [17592186313247 1034 "\\frac{1}{2}" 13194139534832 true] [17592186313247 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534832 true] [17592186313247 1111 #uuid "81d3254d-3bed-51d0-8297-233436b64199" 13194139534832 true] [17592186313248 1000 #edb/ref 17592186313249 13194139534832 true] [17592186313248 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139534832 true] [17592186313248 1041 "field-2" 13194139534832 true] [17592186313248 1104 #edb/ref 17592186313249 13194139534832 true] [17592186313248 1110 #uuid "c87fac21-c636-55be-8f97-5c5744f6805a" 13194139534832 true] [17592186313249 1034 "-\\ln(2)" 13194139534832 true] [17592186313249 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534832 true] [17592186313249 1111 #uuid "dd9a4b56-1f5c-5ae0-ba62-c83012a38d2e" 13194139534832 true] [17592186313250 1017 #edb/ref 17592186313251 13194139534832 true] [17592186313250 1089 "q-73335" 13194139534832 true] [17592186313250 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045464 13194139534832 true] [17592186313250 1100 "A particle $P$ is traveling along the $x$-axis with displacement $s(t)$ from a fixed origin $O$ given by\n\n$$\ns(t)=(t+1){e}^{-t},\\,t\\ge 0.\n$$\n\nFind the time at which the acceleration is zero, and find the value of the velocity at this moment." 13194139534832 true] [17592186313250 1113 #uuid "f742d5d3-d314-55a4-a2e7-77b78815a252" 13194139534832 true] [17592186313250 1145 "First, we calculate $v(t)$ by differentiating $s(t):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}s}{\\text{d}t} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}((t+1){e}^{-t}) \\\\  & =-t{e}^{-t}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nNow, we differentiate $v(t)$ to find $a(t):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}t} \\\\  & =\